From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] localspl: printer data sent to CUPS raw

A job to a CUPS port was handed to CUPS as "auto": CUPS guessed its type and
filtered it. A Windows driver's output (the LabelWriter 550's raster
protocol, ZPL, PCL) or a program writing to the printer directly was taken
for text and printed as a page of characters. Data that is not a PostScript
or PDF document now goes to CUPS as application/vnd.cups-raw, straight to
the device; our PostScript driver's jobs are typed as before.

Test: test/cupsdrv-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_CUPSRAW: the job was text/plain).
---
--- a/dlls/localspl/cups.c
+++ b/dlls/localspl/cups.c
@@ -344,6 +344,7 @@ static BOOL cups_write_doc(doc_t *doc, const BYTE *buf, unsigned int size)
     if (doc->cups.state == doc_create_job)
     {
         const char *format;
+        BOOL autotype = FALSE;
         int i, job_id;
 
         doc->cups.num_options = get_cups_default_options(doc->cups.queue,
@@ -356,7 +357,23 @@ static BOOL cups_write_doc(doc_t *doc, const BYTE *buf, unsigned int size)
         if (pcupsGetOption("raw", doc->cups.num_options, doc->cups.options))
             format = CUPS_FORMAT_RAW;
         else if (!(format = pcupsGetOption("document-format", doc->cups.num_options, doc->cups.options)))
+        {
             format = CUPS_FORMAT_AUTO;
+            autotype = TRUE;
+        }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_CUPSRAW
+        /* Stained Glass OS: data that is not a PostScript or PDF document is
+         * the printer's own language (from a Windows printer driver, or a
+         * program writing to the printer directly); CUPS must hand it to the
+         * device untouched instead of guessing a type and filtering it */
+        if (autotype && !doc->cups.restore_ps_header &&
+            !(doc->cups.buf_len >= 2 && !memcmp(doc->cups.buf, "%!", 2)) &&
+            !(doc->cups.buf_len >= 4 && !memcmp(doc->cups.buf, "%PDF", 4)))
+        {
+            TRACE("printer data: sent raw\n");
+            format = CUPS_FORMAT_RAW;
+        }
+#endif
 
         job_id = pcupsCreateJob(CUPS_HTTP_DEFAULT, doc->cups.queue,
                 doc->cups.doc_title, doc->cups.num_options, doc->cups.options);
